  "final_message": "I've fixed the crash and written `answer.json`. The wolfi and chainguard tests pass, 16 in total.\n\nThe cause was `SecDBParser.build_reference_links` in `src/vunnel/providers/wolfi/parser.py`. It passed the result of `vulnerability.build_reference_links` straight to `urls.extend`, and that function returns `None` for ids that aren't `CVE-` or `GHSA-` prefixed. The method now skips the extend when it gets `None`. So `GO-2026-5932` returns only `[f\"{security_reference_url}/GO-2026-5932\"]`, and CVE and GHSA ids keep their links as before.\n\nI didn't add a test for the `GO-` case.\n\nA plain `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` fails here with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'vunnel'`. I ran just the wolfi and chainguard tests with `PYTHONPATH=src`, and I haven't run the full suite.",
